WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.230
Seven countries claim
slices of Antarctica:

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.490
Argentina, Australia,
Chile, France, New Zealand,

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.690
Norway and the UK.

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.770
Some of those claims overlap.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.570
And other countries do not
recognise any claims at all.

6
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.930
In the International Geophysical Year,
scientists from twelve countries worked

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.410
in and around the continent.

8
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.030
Rival claims.

9
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.070
Yet today none of them may
mine there, or test a weapon.

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.030
Why not?

11
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.310
In this mission, you'll see
who makes Antarctica's rules,

12
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.430
and how they are checked without an army.

13
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.010
Then you'll follow a timeline
of agreements protecting seals,

14
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.370
krill and fish, and
judge how well they work.

15
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:47.730
Your mission: explain why no country may
mine Antarctica or test weapons there.
